.TH GARMINAV 2
.SH NAME
garminav \- Garmin's Aviation output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "nmea.m";
include "garminav.m";
garminav := load Garminav Garminav->PATH;
Grouper: import garminav;

init:        fn(n: Nmea);
Grouper.new: fn(): ref Grouper;
d.feed:      fn(b: array of byte): list of ref Nmea->Fix;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Garmin panel or portable aviation GPS (GNS 430 and 530, GTN, the aera
and the aviation GPSMAPs) sends, on an RS-232 port set to
.IR Aviation ,
a group of records once a second for a fuel computer, an autopilot or
an emergency locator: STX, records of a letter and its data ending CR
LF, ETX; 9600 baud.
.I Garminav
reads it, after the GNS 530 installation manual's appendix C.
.B Init
takes a loaded and initialised
.IR nmea (2).
.PP
A
.B Grouper
takes bytes in any pieces;
.B feed
gives the fixes the groups completed.
The records read are
.B z
(GPS altitude, feet),
.B A
and
.B B
(latitude and longitude: a hemisphere, degrees, minutes and hundredths),
.B C
(track),
.B D
(ground speed, knots) and
.B Q
(magnetic variation, a hemisphere and tenths of a degree); the
navigation records (distance, cross track, waypoint, bearing) are
passed over.
The track is magnetic unless the unit is set to true, when its
variation is E00.0; the fix's course is made true with the variation.
A record of dashes is data the unit does not have; a group without a
position is a lost fix.
A group ends at ETX, or at the next
.B z
when the ETX was lost.
A fix has no time: the format gives none, and the caller stamps it.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/garminav.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR nmea (2),
.IR gpsfs (4)
.SH BUGS
The manual leaves open whether a record's fields are separated by
blanks and whether minutes have a decimal point; blanks are ignored and
a point is taken if there is one.
This has been checked against the manual, not against a unit.
